00:00:28.588 --> 00:00:29.505
Key idea.

11
00:00:30.755 --> 00:00:36.131
An ordered set of (score desc, name) gives top-N and neighbours by walking from a position.

12
00:00:36.411 --> 00:00:38.459
Rank needs how many are ahead of me?.

13
00:00:38.739 --> 00:00:45.950
Walking the set is O(n), so keep a Fenwick (binary indexed) tree of counts per score for O(log S) prefix sums.

14
00:00:46.230 --> 00:00:49.750
Redis does this with a skip list whose links carry span counts.

