00:07:00.569 --> 00:07:03.001
Interview, and Production (Spring Boot 4).

106
00:07:03.281 --> 00:07:05.287
TreeMap + Fenwick tree for ranks:

107
00:07:05.567 --> 00:07:21.503
Redis sorted set (skip list + hash): rank queries are built in. one board: one key per board or period (lb:weekly, lb:2026-w03), with EXPIRE for old periods. ties by insertion order:

108
00:07:21.783 --> 00:07:29.271
Redis breaks score ties lexicographically; encode score 10^k + (MAXTS - ts) for first to reach it wins.

109
00:07:30.621 --> 00:07:33.479
Tens of millions of players fit in one sorted set.

110
00:07:33.759 --> 00:07:38.367
Beyond that, shard by score range or region and merge the top-N per shard.

111
00:07:39.717 --> 00:07:40.592
Part 8.

112
00:07:40.872 --> 00:07:41.981
Common mistakes.

113
00:07:43.231 --> 00:07:49.098
Sorting the whole list on every query (O(n log n)), which falls over at millions of players.

114
00:07:49.378 --> 00:07:53.282
Leaving ties ambiguous, so ranks jump around between refreshes.

115
00:07:53.562 --> 00:07:56.591
Changing a score in place inside the ordered structure.

116
00:07:56.871 --> 00:08:00.007
A single global sorted set for 100M players.

117
00:08:00.287 --> 00:08:05.471
Shard by region or league, and compute global top-N by merging the shards' top-Ns.

118
00:08:06.821 --> 00:08:07.717
Part 9.

119
00:08:07.997 --> 00:08:09.341
Follow-up questions.

120
00:08:10.591 --> 00:08:11.466
Question.

121
00:08:11.746 --> 00:08:14.967
How do you get the rank of a player among 500 million?

122
00:08:15.247 --> 00:08:16.613
Thirty-second answer:

123
00:08:16.893 --> 00:08:19.645
An exact rank needs a global ordered index.

124
00:08:19.925 --> 00:08:33.109
Shard by score range (each shard knows its count, so rank = counts of higher shards + local rank), or use approximate ranks from a score histogram, which is often enough when you show top 3%.

125
00:08:34.459 --> 00:08:35.333
Question.

126
00:08:35.613 --> 00:08:37.789
Daily, weekly and all-time boards?

127
00:08:38.069 --> 00:08:39.435
Thirty-second answer:

128
00:08:39.715 --> 00:08:47.075
Keep separate sorted sets per period (lb:2025 to 01 to 01) with TTLs.

129
00:08:47.355 --> 00:08:53.349
Use ZUNIONSTORE to build the weekly board from the daily ones, or update all three on each score event.

